Brainstorming & Ideation Phase

The purpose of this phase is to identify the security problem, understand the access requirements, and design an ACL-based solution before implementing it in ServiceNow.

1. Problem Identification

The project focuses on protecting Institution Details records containing student information such as:

Student Name
Roll Number
Faculty Name
Email
Phone Number
Branch

The main security requirement is to prevent unauthorized users from accessing or modifying these records.

The system should ensure that:

EEE users can access only EEE records.
Users without the required role cannot access the records.
Administrators have complete access.
Different roles provide different permissions.
2. User Requirements
User/Role	Permission
No custom role	No access
bb1	Read EEE records
bb1 + bb2	Read + Create
bb1 + bb2 + bb3	Read + Create + Write
bb1 + bb2 + bb3 + bb4	Read + Create + Write + Delete
Admin	Full access

The permissions are cumulative, meaning each additional role provides an additional operation.

3. Proposed Security Solution

ServiceNow Access Control Lists (ACLs) will be used to control access.

Four types of ACLs are planned:

Read ACL → Controls who can view records.
Create ACL → Controls who can create records.
Write ACL → Controls who can modify records.
Delete ACL → Controls who can delete records.

The Read ACL will use scripted logic because access depends on both the user's role and the record's Branch value.

4. Role-Based Security Design

Four custom roles will be created:

bb1 → Read
bb2 → Create
bb3 → Write
bb4 → Delete

This creates a simple permission hierarchy:

bb1 → bb2 → bb3 → bb4

Additional roles provide additional capabilities.

5. Branch-Based Access

The Branch field will be used as the main condition for record-level security.

The basic logic is:

Administrator → Allow full access

Authorized EEE user → Allow EEE records

Unauthorized user → Deny access

Therefore, the ACL evaluates both:

User Role + Record Branch → Access Decision

6. Institution Details Table

A custom table named Institution Details will be created with fields such as:

Field	Purpose
Student Roll Number	Identifies the student
Student Name	Stores student name
Faculty Name	Stores faculty information
Branch	Identifies ECE/EEE/CSE
Email	Stores email
Phone	Stores phone number
Description	Additional information

The Branch field will contain:

ECE
EEE
CSE

This allows different branch records to be created and used for ACL testing.

7. Testing Plan

The following scenarios will be tested:

bb1 user → Verify that only EEE records can be viewed.
User without a custom role → Verify that access is denied.
bb1 + bb2 → Verify Create permission.
bb1 + bb2 + bb3 → Verify Write/Edit permission.
bb1 + bb2 + bb3 + bb4 → Verify Delete permission.
Administrator → Verify complete access to all records.
8. Expected Outcome

The brainstorming phase establishes a clear security model before implementation.

The final security flow is:

User → Role Verification → ACL Evaluation → Branch Verification → Access Granted / Denied
